          "to": "u",
          "note": "Parallel to the *eː > i change, all Cholan languages raised Proto-Mayan long *oː to short /u/. Together these two changes collapsed the vowel-length distinction in Cholan by merging the long mid vowels with the short high vowels. Documented in Ch'ol, Ch'orti', and Chontal through Kaufman and Norman's comparative Proto-Cholan work."
